    "SO REFUSAL IS REACHABLE AND GENERICITY IS NOT THE REASON IT DOES NOT FIRE. One argument, one shape, two declared positions, two different answers. A String inhabits Map<K, V> for NO instantiation of K and V, so the mismatch is decidable WITHOUT deciding the generic, and the checker demonstrably decides exactly this shape one arm over. The undecidability the diagnostic reports is a property of where it is asked, not of what it was asked. ",

    "WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT ESTABLISH, because this row forbids borrowing evidence across populations and that boundary is respected here. The fixture's population is ARGUMENT SHAPE (a String where a Map is declared), not this row's VARIANT IDENTITY (Record<Second> where Record<First> is declared). Shape mismatch is decidable from the argument alone; variant identity may not be, and nothing here says it is. What transfers is strictly the ceiling: this row may no longer cite the diagnostic's own name as evidence of a permanent limit, because that name is now measured to be reported over at least one decidable population. The rung and the trigger stand as written. ",

    "AND A SECOND ARM OF THE FIXTURE FOUND A SHARPER HOLE THAT IS NOT THIS ROW'S SUBJECT: arm 4 hands the CONCRETE formal an unapplied function -- empty_map rather than empty_map() -- and is silent, in the same compile where arm 3 refuses a String at that identical position. That is a decidable mismatch admitted where the checker is demonstrably deciding, and it has its own home in unapplied_function_value_admitted_at_a_value_position rather than a receipt here. ",

